upgrade:
  - sdk:
      id: simplicity_sdk
      version: "2025.6.0"
    component:
      - script: protocol/bluetooth/component/upgrade_bluetooth_feature_connection.lua
        description: >
          Verify Bluetooth connection role components
      - trigger: bluetooth_feature_external_bonding_database
        description: >
          Component bluetooth_feature_external_bonding_database requires
          psa_its component. Upgrade adds the required component.
        add:
          - psa_its
      - trigger: btmesh_stack
        description: >
          The Bluetooth Mesh stack model configuration data storage format is
          changed in SDK release 9.0.0. The storage format defaults to the new
          btmesh_stack_model_storage_v2 format in new projects.
          Upgrade adds the btmesh_stack_model_storage_v1 component to the project
          to preserve the old format in existing projects which are based on
          previous SiSDK version.
          The new btmesh_stack_model_storage_v2 storage format is superior to
          the old format because it implements the storage in a manner that
          supports more complex firmware updates, but is not backwards-compatible.
          The project can be migrated to the new format by replacing the
          btmesh_stack_model_storage_v1 component with the btmesh_stack_model_storage_v2
          and btmesh_stack_model_storage_v1_to_v2_migrate components.
          The persistent storage migration shall be executed by calling the
          sl_btmesh_model_migration_migrate_models API from sl_btmesh_api.h file
          before the node/provisioner initialization.
          See details in the API documentation.
          If the migration is done then the btmesh_stack_model_storage_v1_to_v2_migrate
          component can be removed from the project in newer application versions.
        add:
          - btmesh_stack_model_storage_v1